      "title": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing",
      "gist": "The classical feedforward model is incomplete because neurons turn out to be multifunctional, whose flexible, context-dependent signals demand routing that synaptic weights alone handle poorly.",
      "question": "Classical model — why is the connectionist view of neurons incomplete? (a critique)"
    },
