      "title": "Oscillations organize neural information",
      "gist": "Oscillations actively shape spiking, organizing and routing information, and can influence neurons rapidly through electric fields rather than synapses, making them suited to top-down control.",
      "question": "Oscillations — how do brain waves organize and control neural information? (an evidence review)"
    },
